# Checking emails on every change

Emails are part of the product. After any action that can send mail (sign-up, save, approve, reject,
payment, invite, password reset, status change), check the tester mailbox.

{{#if has_mailbox}}
Mailbox: **{{mailbox.address}}**, read through the **{{mailbox.connector}}** connector by the lead session.
Test users use aliases like `{{mailbox.example_alias}}`, so every email lands in this one inbox.
Agents can't read the mailbox themselves: they ask the lead through `blocked` with what to look for.
{{else}}
**No tester mailbox is set up yet.** Until it is, list every action that should send an email as
"Not covered: no mailbox". To set one up: a shared inbox that accepts `name+alias@` addresses
(Gmail and Outlook both do), connected to Claude Code through the mailbox connector, then add it in `npm run setup`.
{{/if}}
{{#if has_mobile}}

Push notifications and SMS follow the same checks when the product sends them (arrived, once, right
person, right text, the tap opens the right screen).
{{/if}}

## For each action

1. **Did it arrive?** The expected email arrives within about 10 minutes.
2. **Only once?** No duplicates, and nothing unexpected (one email per save, not one per field; none for a save with no changes).
3. **Right people?** Who should get it, and who should not.
4. **Right template?** Subject, sender, greeting and name, body text, the data it quotes (names, amounts, dates, before and after), who it says did the action.
5. **Do the links work?** Open every button and link, signed in and signed out. Each lands on the right screen.
6. **Consistent?** Same header, footer, logo and tone as the other emails.

## The log

Each lane keeps `EMAILS.md` in the run folder:

| Time | Action | Subject | To | Result |
|---|---|---|---|---|

A missing, wrong, duplicated or broken email is a finding like any other: it needs the screen action
and the delivered email, {{rules.recheck_times}} times.
